    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-tenure-track-qualification-agreement-eng-j2907.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-11 WU Vienna University of Economics and Business combines excellence with responsibility. Its rare triple accreditation by EQUIS, AACSB, and AMBA is a guarantee for the highest quality research and teaching in the fields of business, economics, and business law. WU’s research is characterized by a wide diversity of disciplines practiced at WU, allowing researchers to deal with even the most complex research questions. International cooperation is very important to WU, and we encourage and support both faculty and student mobility. WU is also very aware of its responsibility to its students, faculty, and staff and is committed to gender equality, equal opportunities, accessibility, family-friendly working conditions, and sustainability. The Institute for Accounting and Auditing is looking for an Assistant Professor in Accounting Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting July 01, 2027, or soon thereafter, and limited for 6 years A qualification agreement will be concluded at the start of the employment (§ 27 of the Collective Bargaining Agreement). Pursuant to WU’s Personnel Development Plan, this position can only be fixed-term for up to six years. Once all objectives agreed upon in the qualification agreement have been fulfilled, the employment relationship can be made permanent. Employees who have successfully completed a qualification agreement are classified as associate professors. From an organizational regulation perspective they belong to the group of professors. Three years after successful completion of the qualification agreement, they are entitled to apply for promotion to full professor according to the By-Laws of WU § 43a. We are inviting applications for an Assistant Professor position (tenure track) in the field of financial accounting to join our institute. Members of the recruiting committee will attend the 2026 EAA Talent Workshop in Madrid and conduct interviews with prospective candidates. Candidates interested in this position are encouraged to attend the workshop and meet with us there. What to expect International faculty with a publication record in top tier accounting journals (e.g., The Accounting Review, Journal of Accounting Research, Journal of Accounting and Economics, Review of Accounting Studies). Strong international research network with regular guests from top-tier universities at our conferences and research seminars. Competitive compensation and strong research support, including research funding, data availability, and attractive teaching conditions. Tax incentive for eligible international researchers moving to Austria. Strong ties to business practice, professional associations, and policymakers. Highly motivated students with accounting majors in undergraduate, graduate, and PhD programs. What you have to offer We invite applications from researchers in the field of financial accounting. High-quality research using quantitative methods, with strong potential to publish in top-tier accounting journals. A completed PhD degree or anticipation to complete a PhD degree in the current academic year. Demonstrated active engagement with the international academic community, for example, through collaboration with international coauthors, research visits at other universities, or presentations at leading academic conferences. Candidates must have completed their PhD at a university other than WU or have at least two years of postdoctoral working experience at another university. It is an advantage if they demonstrate international academic experience—such as a PhD from a non-Austrian university or postdoctoral work at a non-Austrian academic institution for at least two years. The ability to teach in English and commitment to excellence in teaching. Required submission materials: C.V. Cover letter Job market paper Research statement Teaching statement Three letters of reference Additional papers (optional) For further information about the position, please contact Professor Zoltán Novotny-Farkas, at zoltan.novotny-farkas@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,980.80 (14 times per year). In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2907). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/2-Research-and-Teaching-Associates-eng-j2912.html": {
      "title": "2 Research and Teaching Associates",
      "description": "Job opportunity 2 Research and Teaching Associates at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! 2 Research and Teaching Associates Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-21 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 6 years The Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, as part of the Department of Management, is dedicated to studying human behaviour in organisations. You are interested in understanding how individuals can craft their jobs and make things happen in organisations, and/or how people can thrive and experience well-being at work, and pass on your findings to students in the classroom? You are also interested in understanding and helping organisations how to manage people in the context of emerging societal and technical developments, such as AI, changing workplace practices and preferences (e.g., WFH), political/economic uncertainty, and sustainability? This position opens doors to either an academic career or a later switch to a career in business. What to expect Research with Impact: The Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour focuses on timely issues related to positive behaviours in organisations. This means we examine how and when individuals will engage in positive behaviours and contribute to their organisation, as well as experience well-being and meaning in their work, particularly in the context of social and technological developments. You will make a valuable contribution to this research by supporting projects and academic publications. Writing a dissertation: You will conduct research within OB on a topic that is close to your heart, while spending a minimum of one third of your working time to writing your dissertation. Working in a team: At the Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, collaboration and mutual support are priorities. Together, we make a significant contribution to the advancement of our field. Building a lasting network: You will attend and co-organise international conferences and engage in dialogue with research partners and peers. Teaching students: You will plan and conduct courses in Organisational behaviour, for example in the existing SBWL programme of the institute (on the BSc level). You will also contribute to the administration of exams and evaluations. Advising students: You will be available to answer students’ questions, provide feedback on seminar papers, and serve as a co-advisor for bachelor’s theses. Performing organisational tasks: You will assist in the organisation of teaching, research and university life. What you have to offer Academic degree: You hold a diploma/master’s degree in Business Administration, Management, or a related subject area, with a focus on Organisational Behaviour, or in Work & Organisational Psychology, that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU. Passion for research: You are motivated to delve into socially relevant research questions and publish your work in prestigious journals. Content expertise: You have solid knowledge in the area of organisational behaviour. Methodological skills: You have a solid knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methods and the relevant software (such as Mplus, R, SPSS, or Stata, NVivo, or Atlas) for conducting empirical analyses. Language skills: You have excellent German and English skills and can express yourself very well in both languages, orally and in writing. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are capable of and willing to teach courses in German using multimedia formats. Personal qualities: You are curious, interested, and proactive. You can work independently but are also willing to contribute cooperatively as part of a team. Required submission materials (as one PDF file, in this order): Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV Transcripts of grade reports Contact information for 2–3 work and/or academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail) Additionally (as a separate PDF file): Full Master’s/Diploma thesis If available: teaching evaluations If available: research paper We are looking forward to hearing from you! If you have any questions regarding the position or application documents, don’t hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Uta Bindl at uta.bindl@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 21, 2026 (ID 2912). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2913.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-10-21 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 3 years The Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, as part of the Department of Management, is dedicated to studying human behaviour in organisations. We particularly focus on research questions that relate to promoting positive behaviour in organisations and that enable individuals to reach their full potential and experience greater well-being at work. We also consider the contextual embeddedness of human behaviour at work, by studying the impact of emerging societal and technical developments and grand challenges, such as AI, changing workplace practices and preferences (e.g., WFH), political/economic uncertainty, and sustainability, on (positive) human behaviour in organisations. If these topics excite you, we look forward to receiving your application for the advertised position. What to expect Conduct research: You will actively contribute to the institute’s research projects on organisational behaviour and further develop your own ideas. Teach and support courses: You will teach and support courses in OB, for example in the existing SBWL programme of the institute (on the BSc level) as well as in the Department of Management’s Master programme. Supervise master’s and bachelor’s theses: You co-supervise master’s and independently supervise bachelor’s theses. Support organisation and administration: You will help fulfill the institute’s administrative responsibilities. Work as part of a team: You will join a team of committed researchers who collaboratively advance research projects. Benefit from a strong research environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. What you have to offer Doctoral degree: You have successfully completed your doctoral degree in Business Administration, Management, or a related subject area, with a focus on Organisational Behaviour, or Work & Organisational Psychology, and demonstrate a strong commitment to research through promising publication projects. Peer-reviewed presentations at academic conferences and initial publications in journals listed on the WU Star Journal List or the Department of Management Journal List are an advantage. Passion for research: You are highly motivated to pursue an academic career and aim to publish your work in reputable scholarly journals. Relevant expertise and experience: You bring knowledge in areas that meaningfully connect with the focus of the Institute, such as investigating positive behaviours at work (e.g., motivation, proactivity/job crafting), or affect/well-being/meaningfulness in organisations. Ideally, you also have experience in studying human behaviour ‘in context’. Research methodology: You have in-depth training in quantitative methods including experience with common software tools (e.g., Mplus, R, Stata, SPSS) and/or qualitative research methods (e.g., grounded theory, thematic analysis). You have a clear understanding of the strengths and limitations of different methodological approaches. Ideally, you have some experience in using multi-method approaches in field research. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Teaching in German: You are also able and willing to teach courses in German. International experience and language skills: You can demonstrate international exposure in your studies. Strong English skills (both verbal and written) are mandatory. Digital skills: You are confident using standard software applications (e.g., Microsoft Office, video conferencing tools) and can quickly learn new systems. Engagement: You work independently, are organised, take initiative, and are excited to contribute as a team player. Required submission materials (as one PDF file, in this order): Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV Personal statement (briefly outlining research, teaching, and service activities; max 3 pages) Contact information for 2–3 academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail) Copies of 1–2 research papers If available: teaching evaluations Transcripts of grade reports Additionally (as a separate PDF file): Full PhD thesis We are looking forward to hearing from you! If you have any questions regarding the position or application documents, don’t hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Uta Bindl at uta.bindl@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 21,2026 (ID 2913). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2914.html": {
      "title": "Assistant professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Nonprofit Management and Governance Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting March 1, 2027, or later (subject to negotiation), and ending after 2.5 years, no later than September 29, 2029. At the Institute for Nonprofit Management and Governance, we conduct research and teach on the governance and management of nonprofit organizations and social enterprises, on the civic engagement of citizens, and on the nonprofit sector as a whole. We share our findings with the scholarly community, with nonprofit practice, and with our students. The institute’s research has appeared in leading journals in nonprofit studies, management, and sociology. The postdoctoral researcher will join the institute’s work on the societal effects and embeddedness of nonprofit organizations. Current projects include research examining the relationship between nonprofits and their urban environments in cities worldwide, the social innovativeness of cities, and nascent work on the political backlash against nonprofit organizations. We are looking for a researcher who will contribute substantially to this line of work while developing an independent research agenda. What to expect Research: You will contribute actively to the institute’s research projects on nonprofit organizations and their effects on society, and you will develop your own research agenda with the aim of publishing in leading international journals. Teaching: You will independently teach courses on organizations, the nonprofit sector, and social impact in Europe and beyond. Teaching is in English; teaching in German is welcome but not required. Thesis Supervision: You will give students feedback and help them develop their work, including co-supervising master’s theses and independently supervising bachelor’s theses. Organizational and Administrative Tasks: You will share in the institute’s administrative responsibilities, including the organization of international research workshops on topics of mutual interest, and you will help prepare applications for collaborative grants. Collaborative Teamwork: You will join a team of researchers in nonprofit and organization studies who advance research projects together and who support you in developing your own projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. What you have to offer Academic Background: You have completed, or are close to completing, a doctoral degree in management, sociology, nonprofit and public management, urban planning, or a related field. The doctoral degree must be in hand at the start date of the contract. Research Record: You demonstrate a strong commitment to research through promising publication projects and experience in scientific research projects. Peer-reviewed conference presentations and initial publications in journals listed on the WU Star Journal List or the Department of Management Journal List (both accessible online) are an advantage. Subject Expertise: Your work addresses the societal effects of nonprofit organizations. Knowledge of nonprofit management and governance, social entrepreneurship and innovation, urban governance, or the civic dynamics of place-based communities is an advantage. Research Methods: You have a strong empirical research profile with experience in quantitative and qualitative analysis. We expect deep knowledge in one method, but experience with mixed methods and computational social science, including natural language processing, is welcome. Teaching: You are willing and prepared to teach in the areas of nonprofit management and social innovation. Prior experience teaching at the university level and familiarity with multimedia teaching and learning formats are an advantage. Language Skills: Strong English skills are essential. German is not required but is an advantage. Engagement: You work independently, take initiative, and act as a team player. You are willing to organize research events such as workshops and professional development sessions, and you take an active part in scholarly communities such as AoM, ISTR, ARNOVA, ASA, and SASE. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Want to join the WU? Please submit the following materials as a single PDF file, in this order: Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV, indicating when you were or will be awarded your PhD Research statement (max. 2 pages) Teaching statement (max. 2 pages) and, if available, evidence of teaching excellence Contact information for two to three academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail); references will be contacted for shortlisted candidates One or two writing samples, ideally solo- or first-authored working papers or publications Please also submit your full PhD thesis as a separate PDF file. Application documents may be submitted in English or German through the WU online application tool (Reference number: [ID 2914]). Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis starting October 28, 2026, until the position is filled. For questions about the position or the application documents, please contact Prof. Christof Brandtner at christof.brandtner@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2914). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Fachkraft-Universitaetsbibliothek-Benutzungsmanagement-de-j2908.html": {
      "title": "Stellenangebot Fachkraft Universitätsbibliothek (Benutzungsmanagement) bei think:impact",
      "description": "Stellenangebot Fachkraft Universitätsbibliothek (Benutzungsmanagement) bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. Um Ihnen einen bestmöglichen Service zu bieten und die Verwendung mancher Funktionen zu erleichtern, verwenden wir Cookies. Mit der Nutzung dieser Seite erklären Sie sich mit der Verwendung von Cookies einverstanden. Die Einwilligung kann jeder Zeit mit Wirkung für die Zukunft widerrufen werden. Mehr Informationen darüber, welche Daten gespeichert werden, erhalten Sie hier. . Ja, ich bin einverstanden Cookies anpassen Ablehnen DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zurück Jetzt bewerben! Fachkraft Universitätsbibliothek (Benutzungsmanagement) Wirtschaftsuniversität Wien Büro, Verwaltung, Sachbearbeitung Vollzeit Publizierung bis: 21.10.2026 Sie wollen mit Ihrer Arbeit etwas bewegen, Verantwortung übernehmen und so die Rahmenbedingungen für Spitzenforschung und -lehre schaffen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten können. An einer der größten und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversitäten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualität auch Lebensqualität ist. Wir suchen Verstärkung in der Universitätsbibliothek Vollzeit, 40 Stunden/Woche Ab 02.11.2026 Sie wollen kommunikativer Mittelpunkt des Bibliothekszentrums sein? Mit unserem Team die WU-Studierenden, Mitarbeitenden und andere Bibliotheksnutzer*innen bei der Mediennutzung unterstützen? In dieser Funktion innerhalb der Abteilung Benutzungsmanagement servicieren und beraten Sie alle Bibliotheksnutzer*innen bez. Entlehnung und Benutzung. Was Sie erwartet Bibliotheksnutzer*innen servicieren und betreuen: Sie machen Servicedienst am Bibliotheksempfang und stellen Bibliotheksausweise aus. Sie sind erste Ansprechpartner*in der Bibliothek und erteilen Auskünfte rund um Entlehnung und Benutzung Medienentlehnung: Sie führen Entlehnungen im Bibliothekssystem Alma durch Printmedien betreuen: Sie adjustieren Medien, stellen sie ins Regal und heben sie aus. Sie bereiten Medien für den/die Buchbinder*in vor Datenmanagement im Bibliothekssystem Alma: Sie kümmern sich um die Datenpflege und halten Benutzer*innen- und Exemplardaten aktuell Im Team arbeiten: Im Benutzungsmanagement erwartet Sie ein Team von 12 Personen, mit denen Sie gemeinsam die Entlehnung und Benutzung koordinieren Dienste zur Abdeckung von Öffnungszeiten und Samstagdienst: Sie übernehmen im Anlassfall auch Servicedienste von Kolleg*innen und versehen Dienst an einigen Samstagen Was Sie mitbringen Einschlägige Ausbildung/Berufserfahrung: Sie haben die Lehre zur/zum Bibliotheksassistent*in abgeschlossen oder haben Berufspraxis im Bibliotheksbereich oder einem vergleichbaren Umfeld Ausgeprägte Dienstleistungsorientierung: Sie pflegen einen freundlichen, kompetenten und serviceorientierten Umgang mit allen Bibliotheksnutzer*innen Selbständig, teamfähig und sicheres Auftreten: Sie sind eigeninitiativ, haben ein sicheres Auftreten, erkennen, wo man anpacken muss und haben gleichzeitig Freude an der Zusammenarbeit mit unterschiedlichsten Charakteren Sprachkompetenz: Sie haben gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift, weitere Sprachen sind willkommen Zahlenaffin: So gut, wie Sie mit Worten umgehen können, schaffen Sie das auch im Umgang mit Zahlen IT-Anwendungskenntnisse: Sie sind sicher im Umgang mit IT-Systemen wie z.B. MS Office Verlässlichkeit und Genauigkeit: Sie sind bei sämtlichen Aufgaben verlässlich und genau Was wir Ihnen bieten 6 Wochen Urlaub/Erholungszeit Flexible Arbeitszeiten im Rahmen der Gleitzeit Vielfältiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt über Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielfältigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit über 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute öffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr darüber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt beträgt 2.581,20 Euro brutto. Tätigkeitsbezogene Vordienstzeiten können zu einem höheren Einstiegsgehalt führen. Darüber hinaus bieten wir eine Vielzahl an attraktiven Sozialleistungen an. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis spätestens 21.10.2026 (Kennzahl: 2908). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Die WU schätzt Diversität und Inklusion und bemüht sich aktiv um ein vielfältiges Team. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterstützt. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Cookieeinstellungen Close Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind für die Funktionalität unserer Website erforderlich\nund können in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgewählt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen über unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. Wählen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch können Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. Wählen Notwendige Cookies sid Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 1 Stunde Enthält eine anonyme Nutzer-ID, um mehrere Anfragen eines Nutzers derselben HTTP-Session zuordnen zu können. cookieconsent_status Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Tage Dieses Cookie speichert Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen für diese Website. Webstatistik _pk_id* Domainname: job